# Pilotage + language-model agent on claw.local — state at 2026-09-18 (phase 4)

## Try it

Fly the agent from the browser viewer (the agent is a module of the client):

```
ssh claw.local 'zsh -l ~/rlcd/web_sim_up.sh; zsh -l ~/rlcd/web_sim_wait.sh'     # session + model gateway (gemma4:e4b)
ssh -f -N -L 8099:127.0.0.1:8099 -L 8098:127.0.0.1:8098 claw.local               # on the machine with the browser
# open: http://localhost:8099/index.html?host=claw.local&port=4433&cert=<sha-256 from web_sim_wait>&autoconnect=1&agent=http://localhost:8098
ssh claw.local 'zsh -l ~/rlcd/web_sim_down.sh'
```

In the page: push "Engage agent", then a preset or type an instruction. Any flight key, stick or safety press takes control back.
Automated run of the same thing (headless Chrome, truth from Gazebo): `node ~/rlcd/e2e/e2e-agent.mjs <cert> <outDir>` on the machine with Chrome.
Headless live demo (no browser): `ssh -t claw.local 'zsh -l ~/rlcd/live_demo.sh'`.

The session scripts start from `~/Pilotage-agent-web`. That worktree is at the merged content; `main` has the same code.

